From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PoB-Enhanced <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Don't treat unlisted weapon types (Sceptre) as two-handed

When an item replaces the main hand in a what-if calculation, calcs.initEnv drops the off hand unless the new
weapon is one-handed. It decides that with `not weaponTypeInfo[type].oneHand`, treating a type missing from
data.weaponTypeInfo as two-handed. Sceptres are not in that table, so every what-if that put a Sceptre in Weapon 1
silently dropped the off hand: swapping a Sceptre for an identical one cost a build its Focus (and everything the
Focus gives, e.g. 49% of a spell build's damage).

Only treat a weapon as two-handed when the table lists it and says so.
---
 src/Modules/CalcSetup.lua | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/Modules/CalcSetup.lua b/src/Modules/CalcSetup.lua
index 95b78f6bc..ccffe615e 100644
--- a/src/Modules/CalcSetup.lua
+++ b/src/Modules/CalcSetup.lua
@@ -1226,7 +1226,8 @@ function calcs.initEnv(build, mode, override, specEnv)
 				item = build.itemsTab.items[slot.selItemId]
 			end
 			-- if we are replacing the main hand weapon, we should unequip the off hand weapon if it's not allowed
-			local overrideTwoHand = override.repItem and override.repItem.base.type and not (env.data.weaponTypeInfo[override.repItem.base.type] or {}).oneHand
+			local overrideInfo = override.repItem and override.repItem.base.type and env.data.weaponTypeInfo[override.repItem.base.type]
+			local overrideTwoHand = overrideInfo and not overrideInfo.oneHand
 			if overrideTwoHand and override.repSlotName and override.repSlotName:match("^Weapon 1") and slotName:match("^Weapon 2") then
 				local allowLordOfTheWilds = lordOfTheWilds and override.repItem.base.type == "Talisman" and item and item.base.type == "Sceptre" and item.rarity ~= "UNIQUE" and item.rarity ~= "RELIC"
 				local allowInstrumentsOfPower = instrumentsOfPower and override.repItem.base.type == "Staff" and item and item.base.type == "Focus"
